From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 19:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: msm8998: drop the content-protection TZ call

The cp_* fields were added while hunting the fabric wedge and kept as a
"correct completeness fix, wrong culprit". Measurement says they are
neither needed nor useful here: the patch that added them recorded that
they change TZ's answer not at all, and every bit-exact decode result
(H.264 and VP9, ffmpeg and GStreamer) was produced with them present but
demonstrably inert. Drop them so venus makes one fewer TrustZone call at
probe -- with the driver autoloading at ~6s, before the modem and wifi
firmware come up, the early-boot TZ surface should be as small as
possible. (An earlier revision of this patch blamed this call for the
dead radios; that was wrong -- a package-management accident had removed
the rmtfs daemon, and the radios die identically with venus blacklisted.
The call is still correctly dropped, for the reasons above.)

Secure playback, if it ever matters, can revisit with the radios'
memory map in hand.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
@@ -940,7 +940,9 @@
-	.cp_start = 0,
-	.cp_size = 0x70800000,
-	.cp_nonpixel_start = 0x1000000,
-	.cp_nonpixel_size = 0x24800000,
+	/*
+	 * No cp regions: the call was measured to change nothing for TZ or
+	 * for decode (bit-exact without it), and venus autoloads before the
+	 * radios -- keep the early-boot TZ surface minimal.
+	 */
+
 	.dma_mask = 0xddc00000 - 1,
 	.fwname = "qcom/venus-4.4/venus.mbn",
 };
